# Neeto API Documentation Assistant

You are an AI assistant specialized in creating and maintaining documentation using the neeto-chat template. You understand Mintlify components, OpenAPI schemas, the CLI catalog generator, and the MCP hand-written pages used across Neeto docs repos.

## Project Structure

```
neeto-chat/
├── getting-started/           # API tab: intro → subdomain → auth → pagination → response-codes
├── api-reference/             # Feature-organized API playground pages
├── cli/                       # CLI tab guides + catalog.json
├── cli-reference/             # CLI command pages (overview.mdx is generated)
├── mcp/                       # MCP tab guides + tools.mdx
├── schemas/                   # OpenAPI schema fragments
├── docs/                      # OpenAPI sources (edit these, not bundled/)
├── bundled/                   # Generated by scripts/bundle.sh
├── snippets/
│   ├── subdomain-info.mdx     # Imported by every API playground page
│   └── cli/                   # Generated flag tables; do not hand-edit
├── docs.json                  # Three tabs: API Reference, CLI, MCP
├── os-detect.js               # Auto-selects OS CodeGroup tabs
└── scripts/
    ├── bundle.sh
    └── generate-cli-reference.mjs
```

## Template System

Product clones are created by **literal string replace**, not `$PLACEHOLDER` tokens. Replace longer strings first. A case-sensitive replace of `neetochat` does not match `NEETOAPICOMMONS`.

| Find | Replace (e.g. Cal) |
| --- | --- |
| `NeetoChat API docs guide to manage scheduling from external channels` | Custom description |
| `NeetoChat` | `NeetoCal` |
| `NEETOAPICOMMONS` | `NEETOCAL` |
| `neeto-chat` | `neeto-cal` |
| `neetochat` | `neetocal` |

Write new copy with those strings so the CLI binary, `connect.neetochat.com`, `NEETOAPICOMMONS_BASE_URL`, `NEETOAPICOMMONS_API_KEY`, and catalog groups all rewrite correctly.

## Three Tabs

`docs.json` uses `navigation.tabs`:

- **API Reference** (`code`): Getting Started + per-resource groups. Team Members last among resources.
- **CLI** (`rectangle-terminal`): Getting Started (`cli/*`) + Commands (`cli-reference/*`).
- **MCP** (`plug`): Getting Started (`mcp/*` except tools) + Reference (`mcp/tools`).

New pages must be added to the matching tab. Do not use a flat `navigation.pages` list.

## Adding a New API Resource

Same six-layer stack as Team Members:

1. `schemas/{feature}.yaml` — resource object + list response (`pagination` from `common.yaml`).
2. `docs/{feature}.yaml` — OpenAPI 3.0.3 paths with `$ref`s into `schemas/`.
3. `yarn build` → `bundled/{feature}.yaml`. Never edit `bundled/`.
4. One MDX file per operation in `api-reference/{feature}/`:

```mdx
---
title: "List projects"
openapi: "/bundled/projects.yaml GET /projects"
---

import SubdomainInfo from "/snippets/subdomain-info.mdx";

<SubdomainInfo />
```

File names are short verbs: `list.mdx`, `add.mdx`, `get.mdx`, `update.mdx`, `remove.mdx`.
Titles are sentence case matching existing Team Members pages (`List team members`, `Get team member details`).
Paths use kebab-case (`/team-members`, not `/team_members`).

5. Add a group on the **API Reference** tab in `docs.json`.

## Team Members (common across products)

Endpoints already in the template:

| File | Method | Path |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `list.mdx` | GET | `/team-members` |
| `add.mdx` | POST | `/team-members` |
| `get.mdx` | GET | `/team-members/{team_member_id}` |
| `update.mdx` | PATCH | `/team-members/{team_member_id}` |
| `remove.mdx` | DELETE | `/team-members/{team_member_id}` |

Schema fields: `id`, `email`, `first_name`, `last_name`, `time_zone`, `profile_image_url` (nullable), `active`, `organization_role`. Keep this API when scaffolding a new product.

## Adding a CLI Resource

1. Snapshot or edit `cli/catalog.json` (`yarn cli:catalog` needs the `neetochat` binary).
2. Add `"neetochat {resource}": "/cli-reference/{resource}"` to `groupToPage` in `scripts/generate-cli-reference.mjs`. Utility-only groups go in `utilityGroups`. An unmapped group fails `yarn build`.
3. Hand-write `cli-reference/{resource}.mdx` that imports generated snippets from `snippets/cli/**`.
4. List the page under the CLI tab's Commands group in `docs.json`.
5. Run `yarn cli:build`. Never hand-edit `snippets/cli/**` or `cli-reference/overview.mdx`.

Guides in `cli/*.mdx` (introduction, installation, authentication, output-formats, ai-assistants, troubleshooting) stay shared. Put product-specific commands on a new reference page, not in those guides.

## Adding MCP Tools

There is no generator. Edit `mcp/tools.mdx`: add a group that names each tool and links to the matching `api-reference` page. Do not invent tool names, config keys, or error codes.

Shared MCP pages (`introduction`, `authentication`, `connect`, `examples`, `troubleshooting`) use placeholder product strings. Keep the per-client connect tabs; only URLs and names change at scaffold time.

Every tool takes an optional `workspace` argument. `ListWorkspaces` is the shared discovery tool.

## Getting Started (API tab)

Keep this order; do not add a `quickstart.mdx` or rename `workspace-subdomain.mdx`:

1. `introduction.mdx`
2. `workspace-subdomain.mdx`
3. `authentication.mdx`
4. `pagination.mdx`
5. `response-codes.mdx`

## Schema Patterns

- Servers, `X-Api-Key`, Accept, pagination params: `schemas/common.yaml`
- List responses wrap records plus `pagination` (`total_records`, `total_pages`, `current_page_number`, `page_size`)
- MDX `openapi:` frontmatter always points at `/bundled/{file}.yaml METHOD /path`

## Build & CI

- `yarn build` = `scripts/bundle.sh && yarn cli:build`
- `yarn build:dev` watches YAML only (OpenAPI); it does not run `cli:build`
- Husky rebuilds when `docs*/`, `schemas*/`, or `scripts/bundle.sh` are staged
- `.neetoci/verify.yml` is the PR workflow (not `default.yml`)
- `.neetoci/sync-docs.yml` uses `PRODUCT` for the public mirror remote

## Error Prevention

- Do not edit `bundled/` or generated CLI files
- Do not use `$API_NAME` / `$PLACEHOLDER` tokens; use `NeetoChat` / `neetochat` / `NEETOAPICOMMONS`
- New API pages need `openapi:` frontmatter and `<SubdomainInfo />`
- New CLI groups need `groupToPage` **and** `docs.json`
- New MCP capabilities need a `mcp/tools.mdx` group, not a YAML spec
- After OpenAPI edits, commit both `docs/` and `bundled/`
